WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.880
We have to find the HCF and LCM of 18, 20 and 30.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.560
How do we find the HCF and LCM of three numbers together?

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.020
The best way to do it is by reducing all numbers

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.000
to its prime factors.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.100
And then write them in exponential form.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.840
Let's reduce 18 to its prime factors first.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.300
It is Divisible by 2,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.300
2 times 9 is 18, and 3 times 3 is 9.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.880
So 18 can be written as a product of these three  numbers.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.900
So 18 will equal 2 times 3 times 3.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:02.360
In exponential form it can be written as '2 multiplied by 3 squared'.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.260
Let's move on to the second number which is 20.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:13.240
It is Divisible by 2, and the Quotient is 10 which is also Divisible by 2.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:19.300
2 times 5 is 10. We stop here as we got a prime number.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.580
20 can be written as 2 times 2 times 5

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:29.640
And in exponential terms, can be written as 2 squared multiplied by 5.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:37.700
And the last number is 30. It is Divisible by 2 and 2 times 15 is 30 .

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.600
3 times 5 is 15.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.400
So we can write 30 as 2 times 3 times 5.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.100
And in exponential form as well it is written in the same way !

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.100
Now that we have written all three numbers,

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:58.240
in exponential form we can move on to find the HCF and LCM .

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:04.300
To find the HCF we multiply the smallest powers of shared factors.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.140
So let's find the HCF first.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.220
Shared factors are the prime factors that are present in all the numbers.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.360
There are three factors that we have to consider!

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.500
2 ,3 and 5.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:24.240
And out of these, 2 is the only factor present in all the numbers.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.000
Now let's look at the powers of 2.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.140
We have '2 raised to 1',

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.540
'2 raise to 2' and '2 raised to 1' again .

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:37.180
The smallest power is '2 raised to 1.'

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.640
So our HCF will be 2.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.780
How do we find the LCM now?

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.920
To find the LCM, we multiply the highest powers of each factor.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.060
For the LCM the factors do not have to be shared.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.620
First, let's look at 2,

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:59.600
2 squared is the highest power amongst these 3.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.440
So we write 2 squared first .

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.760
Among 3 and 3 Squared, 3 squared is higher.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.920
We multiply this with 3 squared.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.460
Notice that 3 is not present in here.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.300
It doesn't matter.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.540
For the LCM we consider the highest power of each factor

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:22.460
whether it is shared or not !

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.340
And the last factor is 5.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.440
We have 5 raised to 1 here as well as here.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.000
So we multiply this with 5 as its highest power.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.860
This is 4 multiplied by 9 multiplied by 5.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.240
That equals

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.580
180.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.340
So if you're asked to find

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.160
the HCF as well as the LCM of three numbers,

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.540
this is the method you should follow.

